    "description": "A flat-headed, crocodile-like fish about 1.5 metres long from the estuaries of Late Devonian Quebec, about 380 million years ago. Its eyes sat on top of its head and it had lost the fins on its back, so it could lurk in the shallows like a crocodile. Its pectoral fin held rows of small finger bones: the oldest known digits, still wrapped in a fish's fin."
